# Myriad (CR 702.116a) with Doubling Season (CR 614.1a): the one token Bot1 chooses to create for Bot3 is doubled, so two tapped
# 1/1 copies enter attacking Bot3 together (the ruling: Bot1 chooses for each token what it attacks - Bot3 has no planeswalker,
# so there is nothing to ask for the second). Bot2 takes the Patrol's 1, Bot3 the two tokens' 2; both tokens are exiled at end
# of combat. Black Lotus (white) and Mox Emerald and Mox Jet pay for Doubling Season, Mox Pearl for the Patrol.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Doubling Season
Wyrm's Crossing Patrol
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Doubling Season.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wyrm's Crossing Patrol.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
[T4 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot3)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Combat.Attackers.Count = 3
? Combat.Attackers = Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2; Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot3; Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot3
[T4 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 19
? Bot3.Life = 18

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Exile.Count = 0
